{"text": "For decades. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Companies have treated data like a sealed box. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> ― valuable, private, and tightly protected. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That instinct made sense. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> What was inside the box. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> ― customer histories, operational insights, proprietary knowledge ―. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Represented control and competitive advantage. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In an industrial economy. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Owning data was power. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> But in the Intelligence Age. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That logic is becoming an obstacle. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Value no longer comes primarily. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> From keeping information. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> But from connecting it. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> ― across functions, partners, and ecosystems ―. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> To enable learning and action in real time. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Holding on to the sealed box today. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Is less like safeguarding an asset. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And more like dragging an anchor. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The companies moving fastest. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Are not just opening the box. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> They are doing something more deliberate. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Opening it just enough. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> To allow data to move, combine, and learn. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> ― securely, selectively, and with purpose. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The objective is not openness for its own sake. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> But smart connection to gain an edge.", "alignment": {"characters": ["F", "o", "r", " ", "d", "e", "c", "a", "d", "e", "s", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "C", "o", "m", "p", "a", "n", "i", "e", "s", " ", "h", "a", "v", "e", " ", "t", "r", "e", "a", "t", "e", "d", " ", "d", "a", "t", "a", " ", "l", "i", "k", "e", " ", "a", " ", "s", "e", "a", "l",